abstract: >-
  Hands-on spatial analysis with Python in Jupyter notebooks (Google Colab),
  using U.S. Census data as a case study: Python basics, getting ACS data
  through the Census API, cleaning it with pandas, and mapping it with
  GeoPandas. This module was taught as part of the Purdue-NSF GIS
  Cybertraining for the Social Sciences Workshop, a two-day workshop held at
  Purdue University in 2026, to GIS professionals and instructors (Day 1,
  Session B Python track).
keywords:
  - Python
  - Jupyter
  - Google Colab
  - Census API
  - American Community Survey
  - pandas
  - GeoPandas
